# Membership and VIP

## Purpose

Support the strategy's lightweight Phase 2 MVP recurring-supporter and VIP process using Contact fields, Products, Opportunities, Campaigns, and Tasks—without a custom membership object.

## Process

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[Membership or VIP offer Campaign] --> B[Add eligible/target fans]
  B --> C[Fan purchases membership or VIP Product]
  C --> D[Closed Won Opportunity updates fan profile]
  D --> E[Set membership tier/status/renewal or VIP fulfillment]
  E --> F{Renewal approaching or benefit due?}
  F -- Yes --> G[Create one owned reminder/fulfillment Task]
  F -- No --> H[Continue active relationship]
  G --> I[Renew, fulfill, lapse, cancel, or escalate Case]
  H --> I
  I --> J[Refresh renewal/churn and supporter reports]
```

## Desktop wireframe

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  H[Supporter Program<br/>Fan - Current Membership Tier - Status - Renewal Date - VIP Eligible]
  H --> V[Value and eligibility<br/>Fan Tier - True Fan Score - Lifetime Revenue - attendance/engagement]
  H --> O[Related purchase/offer<br/>Product - Opportunity - Campaign - fulfillment]
  V --> T[Upcoming work<br/>Renewal reminders - VIP actions - benefit fulfillment - exceptions]
  O --> T
  T --> A[Actions<br/>Create Renewal Task - Add to VIP Campaign - Update Status - Create Case]
```

## Rules

- Activate only when the membership/VIP business model is in scope and prebuild gates pass.
- Membership values are controlled; purchase and external membership platform remain source evidence.
- VIP Eligible creates an audience, not an entitlement by itself.
- One reminder Task per renewal outcome; repeat evaluations must not duplicate work.
- No payment-card data or unnecessary benefit-detail custom objects.

## Acceptance checks

- New, renewed, lapsed/canceled, VIP purchase, and fulfillment-exception paths are traceable.
- Renewal/churn reporting reconciles to fan fields and source Opportunities.
- Fan service issues route to Case Triage without losing membership/purchase context.
